<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14741" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρβύλη</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ], ἡ,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>strong shoe</i> coming up to
			the ankle, <i>half-boot,</i> used by country people, hunters,
			travellers, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				944
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				259
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Or.</u>
				1470
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηλοπατίδες ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Art.</u>
					62
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐταῖσιν ἀρβύλαισιν ἁρμόσας
				πόδα</span>
			<i>with shoes</i> and all, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				1189
			</span></i> (wrongly expld. by <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
			</span></i> as 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίφρος</span>
			, <i>the stand of the charioteer</i>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ba.</u>
				1134
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρμυλα.</span></div>
